Real trace of `tools/net-probe/run-gamma-main.sh` on macOS Intel (no
Xvfb/Wine, native AWT through Cocoa), portable Temurin JDK 25.0.4.1,
against a clean copy of assets/WorldsPlayer/ as the CWD (the real
worlds.ini, with RestartAt=home:GroundZero/GroundZero.world). Goal: start
NET.worlds.console.Gamma.main as it is (no argv) and see how far it gets
on a Mac today. Three independent runs (2026-09-16), the same wall in all
three. Trimmed: the repeated lines
`[NATIVE-MOCK] Transform.makeIdentity()/setGuts(...)/Material.paramChange()`
of the scene setup (default avatar/room) are collapsed, without removing
anything from the start phases (mock, cache, DNS, tables) or the final
exceptions.

